  86:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****       ================================
  87:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****       [..]
ARM GAS  /tmp/cc9wT2OM.s 			page 3


  88:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****         (#) There are two interrupt lines: line 0 and 1.
  89:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****             By default, all interrupts are assigned to line 0. Interrupt lines
  90:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****             can be configured using HAL_FDCAN_ConfigInterruptLines function.
  91:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c **** 
  92:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****         (#) Notifications are activated using HAL_FDCAN_ActivateNotification
  93:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****             function. Then, the process can be controlled through one of the
  94:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****             available user callbacks: HAL_FDCAN_xxxCallback.
  95:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c **** 
  96:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****   *** Callback registration ***
  97:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****   =============================================
  98:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c **** 
  99:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****   The compilation define USE_HAL_FDCAN_REGISTER_CALLBACKS when set to 1
 100:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****   allows the user to configure dynamically the driver callbacks.
 101:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****   Use Function HAL_FDCAN_RegisterCallback() or HAL_FDCAN_RegisterXXXCallback()
 102:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****   to register an interrupt callback.
 103:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c **** 
 104:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****   Function HAL_FDCAN_RegisterCallback() allows to register following callbacks:
 105:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****     (+) TxFifoEmptyCallback          : Tx Fifo Empty Callback.
 106:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****     (+) HighPriorityMessageCallback  : High Priority Message Callback.
 107:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****     (+) TimestampWraparoundCallback  : Timestamp Wraparound Callback.
 108:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****     (+) TimeoutOccurredCallback      : Timeout Occurred Callback.
 109:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****     (+) ErrorCallback                : Error Callback.
 110:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****     (+) MspInitCallback              : FDCAN MspInit.
 111:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****     (+) MspDeInitCallback            : FDCAN MspDeInit.
 112:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****   This function takes as parameters the HAL peripheral handle, the Callback ID
 113:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****   and a pointer to the user callback function.
 114:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c **** 
 115:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****   For specific callbacks TxEventFifoCallback, RxFifo0Callback, RxFifo1Callback,
 116:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****   TxBufferCompleteCallback, TxBufferAbortCallback and ErrorStatusCallback use dedicated
 117:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****   register callbacks: respectively HAL_FDCAN_RegisterTxEventFifoCallback(),
 118:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****   HAL_FDCAN_RegisterRxFifo0Callback(), HAL_FDCAN_RegisterRxFifo1Callback(),
 119:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****   HAL_FDCAN_RegisterTxBufferCompleteCallback(), HAL_FDCAN_RegisterTxBufferAbortCallback()
 120:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****   and HAL_FDCAN_RegisterErrorStatusCallback().
 121:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c **** 
 122:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****   Use function HAL_FDCAN_UnRegisterCallback() to reset a callback to the default
 123:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****   weak function.
 124:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****   HAL_FDCAN_UnRegisterCallback takes as parameters the HAL peripheral handle,
 125:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****   and the Callback ID.
 126:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****   This function allows to reset following callbacks:
 127:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****     (+) TxFifoEmptyCallback          : Tx Fifo Empty Callback.
 128:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****     (+) HighPriorityMessageCallback  : High Priority Message Callback.
 129:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****     (+) TimestampWraparoundCallback  : Timestamp Wraparound Callback.
 130:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****     (+) TimeoutOccurredCallback      : Timeout Occurred Callback.
 131:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****     (+) ErrorCallback                : Error Callback.
 132:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****     (+) MspInitCallback              : FDCAN MspInit.
 133:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****     (+) MspDeInitCallback            : FDCAN MspDeInit.
 134:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c **** 
 135:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****   For specific callbacks TxEventFifoCallback, RxFifo0Callback, RxFifo1Callback,
 136:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****   TxBufferCompleteCallback and TxBufferAbortCallback, use dedicated
 137:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****   unregister callbacks: respectively HAL_FDCAN_UnRegisterTxEventFifoCallback(),
 138:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****   HAL_FDCAN_UnRegisterRxFifo0Callback(), HAL_FDCAN_UnRegisterRxFifo1Callback(),
 139:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****   HAL_FDCAN_UnRegisterTxBufferCompleteCallback(), HAL_FDCAN_UnRegisterTxBufferAbortCallback()
 140:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****   and HAL_FDCAN_UnRegisterErrorStatusCallback().
 141:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c **** 
 142:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****   By default, after the HAL_FDCAN_Init() and when the state is HAL_FDCAN_STATE_RESET,
 143:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****   all callbacks are set to the corresponding weak functions:
 144:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****   examples HAL_FDCAN_ErrorCallback().
ARM GAS  /tmp/cc9wT2OM.s 			page 4


 145:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****   Exception done for MspInit and MspDeInit functions that are
 146:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****   reset to the legacy weak function in the HAL_FDCAN_Init()/ HAL_FDCAN_DeInit() only when
 147:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****   these callbacks are null (not registered beforehand).
 148:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****   if not, MspInit or MspDeInit are not null, the HAL_FDCAN_Init()/ HAL_FDCAN_DeInit()
 149:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****   keep and use the user MspInit/MspDeInit callbacks (registered beforehand)
 150:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c **** 
 151:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****   Callbacks can be registered/unregistered in HAL_FDCAN_STATE_READY state only.
 152:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****   Exception done MspInit/MspDeInit that can be registered/unregistered
 153:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****   in HAL_FDCAN_STATE_READY or HAL_FDCAN_STATE_RESET state,
 154:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****   thus registered (user) MspInit/DeInit callbacks can be used during the Init/DeInit.
 155:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****   In that case first register the MspInit/MspDeInit user callbacks
 156:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****   using HAL_FDCAN_RegisterCallback() before calling HAL_FDCAN_DeInit()
 157:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****   or HAL_FDCAN_Init() function.
 158:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c **** 
 159:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****   When The compilation define USE_HAL_FDCAN_REGISTER_CALLBACKS is set to 0 or
 160:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****   not defined, the callback registration feature is not available and all callbacks
 161:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****   are set to the corresponding weak functions.
 162:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c **** 
 163:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****   @endverbatim
 164:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****   ******************************************************************************
 165:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****   */
